section('## 2. Source code operational contract and irreversible information boundaries')
section('A. **As-of observed candidates:** inherit R13 first occupied 250ms quote, separate all observed distinct milliseconds, verified first actually observed within-bin spread squeeze, past 3s Bid/Ask motion, past 15s/300s EMA, 15s quote-gap reset and 300s warmup. R14 RELIEF_SHOCK_4000 is new: `(250ms_first OR first_observed_squeeze) AND spread<=4.00 AND spread<=0.70*past_300s_spread_EMA AND past_15s_spread_EMA<=past_300s_EMA AND 3s_bid_ask_motion_signs_agree`. This is as-of filter, not BUY/SELL forecast. <=$4 is unsafe/unapproved for runtime. Original <=$1.50 remains source-only control; never silently widened.')
section('B. **Immutable original strict label gate:** at decision quote i BUY enters Ask[i] or SELL enters Bid[i]; favorable BUY future Bid>=Ask[i]+0.12 / SELL future Ask<=Bid[i]-0.12 by 15,000 ms, includes original nominal 0.02 fee; zero adverse on opening liquidation quote over complete 30,000ms, e.g. BUY future minBid > Bid[i]-0.10, SELL future maxAsk < Ask[i]+0.10. Source incomplete/gap>15,000ms = censored. First observation only after entry millisecond. These strict future-known labels select what side *in the lab only*; no runtime classifier developed.')
section('C. **Nine independent simulated observed-quote fill variants:** lag [0,100,500]ms × slippage [0,0.02,0.05] each leg. Fixed original signal at observed quote ordinal i is NOT reselected when lag changes. Entry executes on first observed quote at/after lag, provided <=1000ms freshness and lane-specific fill spread <=$1.50 or <=$4.00; reject otherwise. Original full30 adverse/no-gap/surveillance recalculated from ACTUAL delayed filled liquidation quote and exact 15s favorable target with fee and both slippage legs charged. Outcomes individually 1 strict good, 0 completed failure, -1 rejected, -3 censored. Censor never becomes good. Every full-source candidate-lane contains all nine codes, fill ordinals and exit ordinals.')
section('D. **Robustness retrospective tiers:** source action must be ORIGINAL strict good at original quote then must survive all 9, >=7, >=5 or >=1 independent fill scenarios. These future-stress outcomes are **offline labels only**. For every admitted candidate the interval starts at the original source signal timestamp, and ends at the latest observed first TP among successful scenarios or last fill +30s among completed/censored failed scenarios; rejected variants do not open phantom positions. Each tier applies exact earliest-finish interval scheduling to these known intervals, with strictly greater next-entry timestamp than previous worst-case end. Thus this is conservative multi-scenario occupancy for the *future-known* selected signals, not an executable prospective policy.')
section('E. **Quarter proof:** For each source, lane, tier, all four full 15min UTC buckets reprocessed independently, with optimistic isolated quarter maximum given complete scenario-labeled intervals. Ignoring cross-quarter conflicts makes the independent upper an optimistic bound, not a globally joint optimum. Separate global one-hour max-count schedule counts by quarter and tests source exact quota 28/27/25/24; all four complete quarters remain, including zero candidate/bound failure rows. Quota is a reporting objective; no threshold is dynamically loosened to make it pass.')
